{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1744213,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":null,"paid":0,"title":"Chemi Craft","festival_id":504454,"organization_id":675999,"web_url":"www.techfest26.com\/","start_date":"2026-09-02T18:30:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-17T16:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/chemi-craft-techfest26-annual-technical-festival-of-sliet-sant-longowal-institute-of-engineering-and-techno-1744213","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>All That You Need to Know About Chemi Craft &mdash; techFEST'26<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>About techFEST'26<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>techFEST'26 is North India's premier technical festival, organised by Sant Longowal Institute of Engineering and Technology (SLIET), Longowal, Punjab.<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Registration for the&nbsp;techFEST&rsquo;26 package&nbsp;is compulsory for&nbsp;accommodation and&nbsp;other perks, while&nbsp;participation in individual&nbsp;events is free*.<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong><a href=\"http:\/\/www.techfest26.com\/\">www.techfest26.com<\/a><\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p><strong>Register Now:<\/strong><br \/><a href=\"https:\/\/www.techfest26.com\/package\">https:\/\/www.techFEST26.com\/package<\/a><\/p>\n<p><strong>Website and Email:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Website: <a href=\"http:\/\/www.techfest26.com\/\">www.techfest26.com<\/a><\/li>\n<li>Email: <a href=\"mailto:techfest@sliet.ac.in\">techfest@sliet.ac.in<\/a><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Follow Us for Updates:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Instagram and other social media platforms<\/p>\n<p><strong>For Queries:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Naman Kumar Sinha (Overall Coordinator): +91 78568 93952<\/li>\n<li>Shubham Kumar Singh (Overall Coordinator): +91 97711 74465<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Prepare yourself for a journey of technology, creativity, and celebration.<\/p>\n<p>Mark your calendars and be part of the magic of techFEST'26 at SLIET.<\/p>\n<p>We cordially invite you to Chemi Craft, organised as part of <strong>techFEST'26<\/strong> &mdash; Annual Technical Festival of SLIET. Showcase your talent, compete with the sharpest minds and earn your moment of glory.<\/p>\n<p><em><strong>&ldquo;Get ready to show off your creativity and innovative ideas by making a working model at Chemi-Storm.&rdquo;<\/strong><\/em><\/p>\n<p><strong>About the Event:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Chemi-Craft is an event to portray working and semi-working models related to chemical engineering and allied fields.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Task for Team:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Construct a working or semi-working model based on chemical concepts that demonstrates chemical engineering principles.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Details:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Number of Rounds:<\/strong> 3<\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 1: Abstract Submission<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Format of the Abstract:<\/strong> Title, Participant&rsquo;s Name, Email, Mobile No., College Name, Branch, Registration No.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Abstract (1&ndash;2 pages):<\/strong> The abstract must have an appropriate title, picture and overview of the topic.<\/li>\n<li>The full paper margin line is 1.5 cm.<\/li>\n<li>The abstract must be submitted as a hard copy, a week before the presentation.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 2: Interview Round<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>In the interview round, judges ask questions based on the participant&rsquo;s model.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 3: Model &amp; Working<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Students have to demonstrate how the working model operates.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules &amp; FAQs:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>All the students will be evaluated based on their creative thinking.<\/li>\n<li>All undergraduate and diploma students with valid ID cards of their respective educational institutes are allowed to participate.<\/li>\n<li>The decision of the judges will be final and binding.<\/li>\n<li>Each team can have a maximum of three members.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Judgement Criteria:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Stage 1: Abstract &mdash; weightage 30%<\/li>\n<li>Stage 2: Interview &mdash; weightage 30%<\/li>\n<li>Stage 3: Model &amp; Working &mdash; weightage 40%<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Certification Policy:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Certificates will be provided to all participants.<\/li>\n<li>Certificate of Excellence will be provided to the winners (as per the results declared by the judges).<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Important Note:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The organizers reserve the right to modify rules, prize pool, dates, venue, or timing of the competition under unforeseen circumstances.<\/li>\n<li>All guidelines are subject to change; participants are advised to regularly check the official techFEST'26 website for updates.<\/li>\n<li>Adherence to the latest rules is mandatory for all teams.<\/li>\n<li><strong>The details mentioned in this Problem Statement may be subject to change at any time.<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Additional Team and Safety Rules:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Team size: 2&ndash;3 members.<\/li>\n<li>Only the allowed reagent list may be used; anything outside needs prior approval.<\/li>\n<li>PPE is non-negotiable; violations stop the experiment on the spot.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>For Further Query:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Domain Advisor:<\/strong> Sahil Sinha, 2432067\/GCT, 9065297749<\/li>\n<li><strong>Domain Coordinator:<\/strong> Amit Kumar, 254013105\/GCT, 8010064068<\/li>\n<li><strong>Event Coordinator:<\/strong> Suraj Kumar, 2632004\/GCT, 8709154514<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>General Rules:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>All participants must carry a valid college ID card and their techFEST'26 registration receipt.<\/li>\n<li>Reporting time will be communicated to registered teams; late reporting may lead to walkover.<\/li>\n<li>The decision of the judges and organisers will be final and binding in all matters.<\/li>\n<li>Any form of misconduct, plagiarism or use of unfair means leads to immediate disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>Participants are responsible for their own equipment and personal belongings.<\/li>\n<li>Organisers reserve the right to modify any rule at any time; updates are announced at the venue.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to students of all institutes and all degree programmes (unless specified otherwise in the event rules above).<\/li>\n<li>Participants must be registered for techFEST'26 through the official portal.<\/li>\n<li>Cross-college teams are welcome.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Mark your calendars and be part of the magic of techFEST'26 at SLIET!<\/p>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":null,"registration_clicks":0,"user_id":27463276,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-08-25T21:52:49+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-01T23:23:05+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"general_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"NO1HYAM","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":1,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":null,"checked":2,"display_title":null,"show_discussions_only_user":1,"show_reviews_only_user":1,"show_score_card":0,"players_count":55,"referral_leaderboard_show":0,"is_ad_free":0,"enable_gamify_leaderboard":0,"tpo_college_id":null,"publish_at":"2026-08-27 12:18:46","auto_shortlist_trigger":false,"enable_ai_discussion":false,"total_unlock_teams":0,"enable_hiring_automation":false,"auto_send_participation_certificate":false,"closed_at":null,"linkedInEventId":"","teams":[],"players":[],"logoUrl":"https:\/\/d8it4huxumps7.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/images\/75x75\/uploadedManual-6aad76123c52d_logo_of_techfest.webp","logoUrl2":"https:\/\/d8it4huxumps7.cloudfront.net\/uploads